-# MLBB Heroes — Gusion safety candidate
+# MLBB Heroes — Balmond candidate
 
-This is a distinct Gusion S1 / tower-retreat safety candidate based on the preserved Hanabi v5 + Uranus 60% baseline. It excludes the separate Chou native-movement patch. Earlier candidate archives were not changed.
+A distinct Balmond implementation candidate based on the preserved 1.1.63 source baseline, targeting the TFM2 0.7.0 runtime. It retains the prior Hanabi/Uranus/Gusion/Chou/Zhask work and archives unchanged.
 
-See `RELEASE_README.md` and `GUSION_SAFETY_FIX_VALIDATION_REPORT.md` for exact scope and validation. The source and SDK are included in this source package; the separately delivered runtime ZIP contains no source or SDK.
+- `BALMOND_IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md` — current-kit baseline, TFM2 assumptions, asset mapping, and validation limitations.
+- `Balmond_TFM2_Feasibility_Research.md` is retained in the companion source archive/workspace.
+- `source/balmond/` — atlas/timing mapping and user-provided source/provenance assets.
+- `source/audio/balmond/` — source OGGs; corresponding mono PCM16 WAVs are under `sound/sfx/`.
 
-Gameplay is not yet verified. Passing unit tests and a Windows release build do not establish in-game success.
+The native source includes Balmond's passive and skill handlers, the champion data/localization/style entries, default skill icons, a mapped sprite/animation, separate dash/spin/ultimate VFX, and routed default voice clips. The supplied body-atlas frame index gaps are normalized to measured TFM2 action cycles; the source JSON contains no exact duration values.
+
+The build uses `mod-api-stable` adjacent to this project (or the `TFM2_STABLE_SDK_DIR` environment variable). See the separate runtime ZIP for the source/SDK-free install package. Passing tests and a successful cross-compile do not prove a TFM2 0.7.0 in-game load or match result.
--- a/RELEASE_README.md
+++ b/RELEASE_README.md
@@ -1,14 +1,13 @@
-# Gusion S1 and tower-retreat safety candidate
+# MLBB Heroes — Balmond runtime candidate
 
-Distinct runtime/source candidate based on the preserved Hanabi v5 + Uranus 60% baseline. It excludes the separate Chou native-movement patch and does not modify Chou, Hanabi, Uranus, Zhask, or other hero source code.
+This Windows runtime ZIP is a distinct Balmond candidate targeting TFM2 0.7.0. Keep the extracted `mlbb_heroes` folder intact when installing it through the TFM2 mod loader. The package includes runtime data/assets and the compiled Windows DLL only; it does **not** contain Rust source or the stable SDK.
 
-## Gusion scope
+## Included Balmond content
 
-- Prevent unsafe S1 recast routes from slipping through the native/base AI input after the custom preflight declines them; keep the effect-time safety recheck.
-- Keep the outward tower-escape waypoint latched until the native movement route remains safe for eight consecutive AI ticks; extend outward if it turns unsafe during confirmation.
-- Preserve safe native tower attacks/pushing and existing allied-tanker checks. No Return-home order is added.
-- Preserve Gusion’s existing S2 volley/follow-up logic and logging.
+- Bloodthirst 5%/10% heal events; Soul Lock dash/path damage and slow; Cyclone Sweep timed spin, movement speed and defense-shred stacks; missing-HP true-damage Lethal Counter.
+- User-supplied mapped body sprite/animation, separate skill VFX, default skill icons and the default voice set.
+- English descriptions and champion-view placement entry.
 
-## Validation
+## Validation status
 
-See `GUSION_SAFETY_FIX_VALIDATION_REPORT.md`. Unit/static/build validation is complete; in-game behavior remains unverified. Test with the exact game version and runtime ZIP, and retain the diagnostic log.
+The candidate Rust test suite passes (74 tests), JSON/FAnim/audio references parse, and the Windows x86-64 release DLL cross-compiles. This is static/build validation only. No TFM2 0.7.0 load, match, visual, or audible result has been confirmed. Review `BALMOND_IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md` in the source archive for the assumptions and known fidelity gaps before testing.
--- a/ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md
+++ b/ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md
@@ -34,3 +34,12 @@
 - The Hanabi character atlas and six VFX sprite sheets under `source/hanabi/import_2026-10-28/` were supplied by the user, who identified the VFX workflow as GPT Image 2.5 Sunburst. The candidate preserves those original files unchanged and records derived crops/scales in `HANABI_IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md`.
 - The four 100×100 classic/default Hanabi ability icons in the same import folder were staged as transparent PNGs. Three active-skill icons are wired into the champion data; the passive icon is retained in `icons/` for reference because the project data schema exposes three active action-icon slots.
 - No license or redistribution permission is asserted for Mobile Legends character/icon art or user-supplied generated assets. Confirm rights before public redistribution.
+
+## Balmond candidate assets
+
+- The Balmond body atlas and the `Balmond-spin.png`, Skill 1, Skill 2 ring, and Ultimate art were supplied by the user and are preserved in `source/balmond/` and `source/balmond/reference_effects/`. The generated runtime sprite/VFX animation metadata references these assets without replacing or regenerating the art.
+- The classic/default action icons were fetched from the Mobile Legends Fandom Balmond page. Exact source URLs, byte sizes, and hashes are in `source/balmond/ASSET_SOURCES.json`.
+- The default English Balmond voice set (selection, movement, basic exertion, Ultimate, death) is sourced from https://mobile-legends.fandom.com/wiki/Balmond/Audio. Exact source URLs and mappings are in `source/audio/audio_manifest.json`; original OGG files are retained under `source/audio/balmond/default/` and playback files are converted to mono 22.05 kHz PCM16 WAV.
+- The page supplies voice/grunt clips, not distinct non-voice Skill 1/Skill 2 ability SFX. No voice lines were fabricated.
+
+**Rights warning:** the source references identify provenance only and do not establish permission to redistribute user-supplied images, game art, icons, or game voice recordings. Confirm rights before public redistribution.
